{"kind":"assert","text":"dap-foldkit M2 report on parts 2 to 4 of this request: the foldkit adapter does not need `foldField`, `FieldAlgebra` or a moved `ValueOf`. The planner can now decide parts 2 to 4 on their value inside dap alone.\n\nFiled 2026-11-13 06:59 EST at Hugh's request. Assert `19b7957b` held parts 2 to 4 until this report.\n\n## What M2 found\n\nThe first M2 build had a module L3, `effect-schema`: a private fold of each declared field type into an Effect Schema. Nothing used it. The rework removed it. Three exports of `@generalbusiness/dap-client` at main `64112e45` cover what the adapter needs:\n\n- `shapeDeclaredAct(definition, kind, asked)` checks an act's values at run time and names the failing field.\n- `AskedOf\u003cD, K\u003e` types an act's `on` and `fields` from the definition's own data. An undeclared kind, a missing field and a wrong value each fail to compile.\n- `ValueOf\u003cT\u003e` types an item's values. The adapter builds a `Row\u003cD, T\u003e` type from it.\n\nfoldkit requires a Schema for the Model. The Model holds the engine's view as one opaque value, so no Schema of a field type is needed. The definition is plain data with `as const satisfies DeclaredDefinition`, and its pinned digest did not change.\n\n## What this means for parts 2 to 4\n\n- The adapter gives no reason to export `foldField` and `FieldAlgebra`. The case that remains is the one inside dap: MCP's `schemaOf`, `typeWords`, and the two type-level mappings `ValueOf` and `NativeInputValue`.\n- One `ValueOf` in `packages/contract` (part 4) would still help an adapter a little: it imports the type from the client today, and that works.\n- My recommendation: do not schedule parts 2 to 4 for the adapter. Keep or drop them on the consolidation value alone.\n\n## Evidence\n\nOne observed run in `~/play/dap-foldkit` on 2026-11-13 against dap main `64112e45`: `npm test` reports 10 files and 140 tests, all pass. `npm run typecheck` reports nothing. `npm run app:headless` reports nine checks, all pass, in headless Chrome on the in-memory scope. The authority is dap's test `Ledger`, with no session and no HTTP.\n\n## Other results for the planner\n\n- M2 is done. M3 (a local dap room) needs LOG-1 `e79ccfaf`, which landed at `64112e45`. M3 adds one file to the adapter: a port on dap's transport and `observeScope`.\n- One new request rests on this one: `6fba1c18`, a guard `isItemEffect` in `packages/derive`.\n- Noted and not filed: the adapter's types `Row\u003cD, T\u003e` and `ProposalOf\u003cD, K\u003e`, with their guards, belong beside `AskedOf` in `packages/client` when the replica, the outbox and the engine move there. That move waits for a second application.\n- A review of the first M2 build reproduced five defects in the handling of pending acts. All five were in the adapter, and none was in dap. `~/play/dap-foldkit/PLAN.md` section 12.3 lists them."}